  "Id": 2807,
  "Title": "3D ultrastructural imaging of chromosomes",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Effectiveness of Serial Block-Face Scanning Electron Microscopy in chromosome imaging",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Researchers at "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "AKU-CRM",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "href": "/crm/Pages/home.aspx",
                  "target": "_self",
                  "linktype": "url",
                  "uuid": null,
                  "anchor": null,
                  "custom": {}
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " have analysed the effectiveness of Serial Block-Face Scanning Electron Microscopy (SBFSEM) in investigating the ultrastructure and organisation of chromosomes in the cell and its nucleus. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The review, published in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "DNA",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "italic"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "href": "https://doi.org/10.3390/dna2010003",
                  "target": "_blank",
                  "linktype": "url",
                  "uuid": null,
                  "anchor": null,
                  "custom": {}
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ",",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "italic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " provides a comprehensive analysis of how this microscopy is helping researchers to reveal the 3D organisational structure of chromosomes. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Due to its ability to auto-register images, the reviewers have deemed SBFSEM useful in studying the ultra-structure of chromosomes and their placement in cells. "
          },
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "To further enhance the productivity of SBFSEM, the reviewers have recommended developing new generation backscattered electron detectors and improvement in resin strength to combat the heat generated during high-resolution imaging for better results. They have also suggested developing automated segmentation tools in the software to accelerate the quantitative analysis of chromosome samples."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The review concludes that the SBFSEM technology coupled with super-resolution microscopy and parallel sample imaging could provide comprehensive insight into the 3D genome maps of single cells. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Contributors to this review include Dr Mohammed Yusuf, Professor El-Nasir Lalani and Atiqa Sajid from CRM, and Professor Ian K. Robinson from the London Centre for Nanotechnology, University College London."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Read the full article: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "https://doi.org/10.3390/dna2010003",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "href": "https://doi.org/10.3390/dna2010003",
                  "target": "_blank",
                  "linktype": "url",
                  "uuid": null,
                  "anchor": null,
                  "custom": {}
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
